.TH REBELLION-SERVER 1 "2026" "rebellion 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rebellion-server \- HTTP+JSON API for the rebellion web scraper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rebellion-server
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rebellion-server
exposes rebellion's scrape, crawl and map operations over HTTP so that any
service can use them. Requests and responses are JSON. One thread-safe
scraper client serves all requests; each connection is handled on its own
thread and carries a single request.
.SH ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B GET /health
Liveness and whether a headless browser is available. Never needs a key.
.TP
.B POST /v1/scrape
Scrape one URL: \fB{"url":"https://example.de/"}\fR. Optional fields include
\fBengine\fR (auto, http, browser), \fBonlyMainContent\fR,
\fBincludeHtml\fR, \fBrespectRobots\fR, \fBtimeoutMs\fR, \fBscreenshot\fR and
\fBactions\fR (click, fill, submit, wait_for, scroll, scroll_bottom, wait).
.TP
.B POST /v1/crawl
Crawl one site: \fB{"url":"...","limit":25,"depth":2}\fR.
.TP
.B POST /v1/map
Discover URLs from sitemaps and homepage links: \fB{"url":"..."}\fR.
.PP
POST bodies must be sent with \fBContent-Type: application/json\fR. Errors
are \fB{"success":false,"code":"...","error":"..."}\fR with a matching HTTP
status. See docs/API.md for the full reference.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIaddr\fR
Bind address, IPv4 or IPv6 (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIn\fR
Port (default \fB$PORT\fR, else 8080).
.TP
.B \-\-api\-key \fIkey\fR
Require \fBAuthorization: Bearer\fR \fIkey\fR (or \fBX\-API\-Key:\fR \fIkey\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-private
Allow scraping loopback, private and link-local hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-cors\-origin \fIorigin\fR
Send \fBAccess\-Control\-Allow\-Origin:\fR \fIorigin\fR. Off by default.
.TP
.B \-\-proxy \fIurl\fR
Proxy URL; repeat for a rotating pool.
.TP
.B \-\-proxy\-strategy \fIs\fR
\fBround\-robin\fR (default), \fBrandom\fR or \fBsticky\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIdir\fR
Persistent browser profile directory (cookies and logins persist).
.TP
.B \-\-max\-browsers \fIn\fR
Concurrent headless browsers (default 4). Each costs a few hundred MB.
.TP
.B \-\-crawl\-cap \fIn\fR
Maximum pages per crawl request (default 100).
.TP
.B \-\-max\-conns \fIn\fR
Maximum concurrent connections (default 32); excess requests get 503.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-body \fIbytes\fR
Maximum request body size (default 2097152).
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
No access log.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Debug logging to stderr.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REBELLION_API_KEY
API key, if \-\-api\-key is not given.
.TP
.B PORT
Default port.
.TP
.BR REBELLION_CHROMIUM ", " CHROME_PATH
Chromium binary to use for the browser engine.
.SH SECURITY
The default bind address is loopback. A loopback server without an API key
only answers requests addressed to localhost, 127.0.0.1 or [::1]. Targets on
loopback, private, link-local and CGNAT networks are refused unless
\-\-allow\-private is given.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT stop accepting connections and let running requests
finish (up to 60 seconds) before exiting.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rebellion-server --api-key "$KEY"
curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/scrape \e
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \e
  -d '{"url":"https://www.berliner-volksbank.de/"}'
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR rebellion (1)
